    "https://www.jobs.ac.uk/job/DSN000/academic-tutor-aerospace-engineering": {
      "title": "Academic Tutor – Aerospace Engineering",
      "description": "Academic Tutor – Aerospace Engineering at Sheffield Hallam University Skip to main content Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Recruiters Find a Job Find PhDs Career Advice Jobs by Email Advertise a Job Your Account Recruiters Back to search results Academic Tutor – Aerospace Engineering Sheffield Hallam University - College of Business, Technology and Engineering / School of Engineering and Built Environment Location: Sheffield Salary: £32,080 to £38,784 Hours: Full Time Contract Type: Permanent Placed On: 5th August 2026 Closes: 6th September 2026 Job Ref: 119107 We are looking to appoint an Academic Tutor in Aerospace Engineering to help inspire the next generation of engineers tackling the challenges of air, space and sustainable transportation. The successful candidate will have a broad background in aerospace engineering, with the ability to support students in applying engineering principles, design, analysis and systems thinking to real-world challenges. Experience gained through academic study, industrial practice or other professional activity, and applicable across aerospace, automotive or railway engineering, would be welcomed. Working within the Future Transportation Subject Area, you will contribute to a professional-from-day-one, project-based curriculum through a range of teaching, learning and assessment activities, while supporting module development and curriculum enhancement. The role will primarily support Aerospace Engineering, while also contributing across Automotive Engineering and Railway Engineering in line with teaching and curriculum needs The School of Engineering and Built Environment brings together engineering, construction and surveying, physics and the built environment. With excellent links to industry, we provide applied learning opportunities for students and our graduates perform strongly in the labour market. Emphasis is also placed on Research, Innovation and Knowledge Exchange within the School and there is firm alignment with UKRI priority areas. We are a welcoming community where staff and students are encouraged to develop their careers and make a fulfilling impact. We offer a diverse range of benefits and opportunities to pursue a rewarding and fulfilling career in a supportive environment. The University currently enrols eligible academic staff into the Teachers’ Pension Scheme (TPS), a defined-benefit pension scheme. Should you be enrolled into TPS, each year you will earn a secure pension benefit of 1/57th of your salary and the University will pay pension contributions towards the cost of this pension (currently worth about 29% of your salary). For a salary of £35,000, for example, the University would pay just over £10,000 in the first year of your employment and you would earn a pension of £614 p.a. for that year (payable from your State Pension Age). Further details on TPS can be found here If you’re a member of the Universities Superannuation Scheme (USS) directly before joining us, you can choose to remain in USS instead. We welcome applications for job-share, part-time and flexible working arrangements. To find out more, take a look at our guide to applying . We recommend you download the job description and person specification when you apply, as this will not be available once the job has closed. Accessibility We are committed to ensuring our materials are accessible to all. If you encounter any accessibility barriers or have suggestions for improvement please contact us using our web accessibility report form . Your feedback helps us enhance our accessibility efforts and improve our services. Share on social media We value your feedback on the quality of our adverts.\n            If you have a comment to make about the overall quality of this advert,\n            or its categorisation then please send us your feedback Advert information Type / Role: Subject Area(s): Location(s): Job tools PhD Alert Created Job Alert Cr